# Frontend React Rules

## Structure

- `src/App.tsx` – Routes, providers
- `src/api/client.ts` – API client (`apiFetch`, typed helpers)
- `src/components/` – Shared UI (Layout, etc.)
- `src/pages/` – Page components
- `src/modules/<name>/` – Optional feature modules (auth, basket, etc.)

## Conventions

- Use `apiFetch<T>(path, options)` from `api/client.ts` for API calls
- Functional components; extract hooks for reusable logic
- React Router for routing; `Layout` with `Outlet` for shared shell
- Module pages live in `src/modules/<name>/` with their own api, context, components

## Easy to Debug

- API errors should be traceable from the frontend: use `apiFetch` which surfaces status, message, and backend `detail` when available
- Surface errors to the user (toast, inline message) so issues are easy to track when something fails

## Example: API Call

```typescript
// src/api/client.ts
export async function getItems(): Promise<Item[]> {
  return apiFetch<Item[]>('/items');
}
```

## Example: New Module

- Add `src/modules/<name>/` with `api.ts`, context (if needed), page components
- Register routes in `App.tsx`
- Add nav links in `Layout.tsx` when applicable
